{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1TI",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some will depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits and doctrines of demons;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Speaking lies in hypocrisy, having their conscience seared with a hot iron;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Forbidding to marry, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and commanding",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to abstain from meats, which God hath created to be received with thanksgiving by them who believe and know the truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For every creature of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good, and nothing to be refused, if received with thanksgiving:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it is sanctified by the word of God, and prayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou shalt put the brethren in remembrance of these things, thou wilt be a good minister of Jesus Christ, nourished by the words of faith and of good doctrine, to which thou hast attained.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But refuse profane and old wives' fables, and exercise thyself ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "rather",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to godliness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable to all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For therefore we both labor and suffer reproach, because we trust in the living God who is the Savior of all men, especially of those that believe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These things command and teach.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in deportment, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Till I come, give attendance to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neglect not the gift that is in thee, which was given thee by prophecy, with the laying on of the hands of the presbytery.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take heed to thyself and to thy doctrine; continue in them: for in doing this thou wilt both save thyself, and them that hear thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
